# LIKE/GLOB sites the guard flags as user-derived but that are safe.
#
# Format matches check-d1-inarray-params.allowlist: one `repo-relative/path.ts`
# per line, optionally `:<line>` to pin a single site. `#` starts a comment.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE, 2026-08-26. Every site the guard found was a real defect
# and every one was fixed rather than allowlisted. Keep it that way if you can:
# an entry here accepts a latent 500, and this family has already produced
# 315 production errors across five call sites in 27 days.
#
# Before adding an entry, try the fix — it is usually one line:
#   like(col, `%${x}%`)  →  containsCI(col, x)     from @/lib/db/contains-ci
#
# `containsCI` compiles to instr(lower(col), ?) > 0. It has no pattern-
# complexity ceiling, and `%`/`_` become literal, which is what a person
# typing them into a search box meant anyway.
#
# Add NEW entries only with an explicit reason (and an issue link if it is a
# deferred fix rather than a genuine exception).
